WEBVTT

00:06.680 --> 00:08.141
2020

00:08.141 --> 00:09.645
DECEMBER 5TH

00:09.645 --> 00:12.107
CANADA-STANLEY PARK

00:21.167 --> 00:21.961
Andy!

00:22.336 --> 00:23.421
No problem.

00:25.259 --> 00:27.263
Under will be taking Autumn!

00:40.122 --> 00:43.086
I'm betting on the charged unluck!
Get away, Fuko!

00:44.923 --> 00:45.967
On it!

01:15.108 --> 01:17.029
The future I know...

01:19.701 --> 01:22.957
<i>Hello, Anno-sensei?
It's me, Tahioka.</i>

01:24.001 --> 01:28.134
I know you prefer to stay silent,
so I'll cut to the point.

01:28.134 --> 01:33.228
The first matter is that the manuscripts you
have stored here might have been replaced...

01:33.646 --> 01:37.696
The other is that we need you
to judge this month's contest.

01:37.987 --> 01:39.407
U-Um...

01:39.658 --> 01:43.833
For the first matter, I'll give you a report after
we've done some more investigating.

01:43.833 --> 01:45.670
As for the second,
are you available to judge?

01:45.670 --> 01:48.216
Um... would it be possible to speak with them?

01:48.509 --> 01:49.427
Huh?

01:51.932 --> 01:54.270
I can't do such a thing-

01:54.270 --> 01:55.731
Huh?

01:56.775 --> 01:57.944
Huh?

02:02.119 --> 02:03.037
Huh?

02:05.375 --> 02:06.753
Thank you very much.

02:08.465 --> 02:10.720
<i>Hello, Anno-sensei.</i>

02:11.680 --> 02:14.853
Nice to meet you.
My name is Fuko Izumo.

02:15.353 --> 02:20.865
Would you mind reading my manga?
I would appreciate it very much if you did.

02:21.491 --> 02:25.332
If it's too far for your convenience,
I don't mind coming to you.

02:27.545 --> 02:30.510
You're wasting your breath.
Anno-sensei doesn't speak to others.

02:31.177 --> 02:33.223
I've never even seen them before!

02:33.473 --> 02:34.809
Is it any good?

02:35.477 --> 02:37.857
If it's an interesting read,
then I'll meet with you.

02:38.483 --> 02:42.700
In five hours,
come to the bench at Stanley Park in Canada.

02:43.368 --> 02:44.996
Both of you together.

02:55.560 --> 02:59.609
<i>"To You, From Me" is the manga that served
as a crutch for Fuko to live her life.</i>

02:59.609 --> 03:03.576
<i>Juiz speaks of how the story drawn within
is a prophecy for this world,</i>

03:03.576 --> 03:07.165
<i>and directs Fuko and Andy
to investigate about the author, Anno Un.</i>

03:07.584 --> 03:13.094
<i>By Andy's proposal, Fuko ends up having to draw
a manga as a means to contact the author.</i>

03:13.094 --> 03:16.475
<i>She is at wit's end as she
has never drawn a manga before,</i>

03:16.475 --> 03:20.568
<i>but Andy persuades Fuko that she only has
to think about things that would throb her heart to death.</i>

03:21.027 --> 03:26.412
<i>With a fresh start, Fuko starts facing her own emotions.
This was for the mission,</i>

03:26.412 --> 03:30.921
<i>but also from a will to become able
to call in bigger strokes of unluck for Andy.</i>

03:31.422 --> 03:35.514
<i>With assistance from other members,
Fuko pours her feelings into her manuscript.</i>

03:36.015 --> 03:38.979
<i>The completed title is "Undead + Unluck."</i>

03:38.979 --> 03:41.526
<i>With that in hand,
the pair heads to a publisher,</i>

03:41.526 --> 03:45.951
<i>and succeeds in an exchange of words
with the author Anno Un as planned.</i>

03:46.410 --> 03:49.249
<i>And now, Fuko and Andy head over to Canada.</i>

03:49.249 --> 03:52.507
<i>That's right.
The exact location where I am now.</i>

03:52.590 --> 03:54.594
ANNO UN

04:06.952 --> 04:09.916
I'm sure they said both of us, together.

04:10.458 --> 04:11.586
I see.

04:12.003 --> 04:18.559
I assume they mean the two of us.
In other words, they know about us.

04:20.730 --> 04:25.321
Not only that. It takes roughly nine hours
to fly to Canada on a passenger airplane.

04:25.447 --> 04:29.789
<i>They got the lowdown that Union tech
can get us there in three hours.</i>

04:30.415 --> 04:32.754
They ain't normal any way y'slice it.

04:38.431 --> 04:43.357
I wonder if we'll really be able to meet them.

04:46.363 --> 04:51.541
Anno Un. Age unknown. Sex unknown.

04:51.541 --> 04:55.048
They say no one knows what
they look or even sound like.

04:55.841 --> 04:59.014
<i>Twenty years ago,
they submitted the first chapter of You-Me.</i>

04:59.808 --> 05:03.649
<i>It was published as a one-time special,
but was so popular it immediately won a serial slot.</i>

05:04.191 --> 05:08.491
They only converse with editorial
via silent phone calls and letters, right?

05:08.491 --> 05:10.120
For all of these past 20 years.

05:10.871 --> 05:13.167
Something's clearly strange 'bout that.

05:13.752 --> 05:19.597
Not even the Union's been able to track down
the mysterious masked manga maker.

05:20.181 --> 05:21.685
Color me interested!

05:22.269 --> 05:24.148
We're gonna nab 'em at all costs!

05:24.691 --> 05:25.568
Yeah!

07:17.833 --> 07:19.169
It's autumn.

07:23.177 --> 07:25.181
DECEMBER 5TH

07:29.649 --> 07:32.153
STANLEY PARK, CANADA

07:36.411 --> 07:38.917
5:00 A.M.
(22:00 JAPAN TIME)

07:50.439 --> 07:52.068
Not here yet, huh?

07:53.697 --> 07:54.364
Want some?

07:54.364 --> 07:55.032
Hmm?

07:55.366 --> 07:57.203
What is that?
It looks so good!

07:57.453 --> 08:01.963
A good ol' Canadian delicacy called poutine.
If you're hungry, help yourself.

08:02.213 --> 08:03.090
Okay.

08:08.100 --> 08:09.645
It's sho good!

08:10.689 --> 08:13.194
Now then... should be any minute now.

08:13.194 --> 08:17.285
You know the plan.
If they get hostile with us, it's go time.

08:17.745 --> 08:21.961
And by hostile I mean them pullin' out weapons,
or gettin' too close for comfort.

08:23.380 --> 08:25.259
So if they do, shoot them?

08:25.510 --> 08:27.598
Yeah. Go for the leg first.

08:29.017 --> 08:31.146
I don't wanna have it come to that, but...

08:31.856 --> 08:37.993
...if we're dealing with a Negator or Artifact-wielder,
if we're one step behind, we're dead.

08:38.494 --> 08:40.958
They seem to know 'bout us, too.

08:43.755 --> 08:46.385
"Undead + Unluck", huh?

08:46.678 --> 08:48.305
Yeah! It's got my interest!

08:48.765 --> 08:51.688
But the setup needs work.

08:51.688 --> 08:53.817
This won't get past the series approval meeting,
you know?

08:54.401 --> 08:57.031
<i>They got that close without me noticing 'em?</i>

08:58.242 --> 08:59.745
Anno Un, I presume?

09:00.204 --> 09:02.333
Yup. That's just my pen name, though.

09:02.960 --> 09:06.801
And I know what you two want to know.

09:06.801 --> 09:11.811
What's the reason behind Billy's betrayal?
How to defeat the four UMAs?

09:12.186 --> 09:15.902
Andy's mysterious past.
And lastly...

09:16.445 --> 09:18.867
...how to defeat God.
Sound about right?

09:21.163 --> 09:24.545
Yeah, I know it all.
But there's a price to pay.

09:24.795 --> 09:25.630
Watch out!

09:25.630 --> 09:27.300
Spider... UMAs?

09:27.676 --> 09:30.264
Autumn spawned those things.
Their Juniors.

09:30.974 --> 09:33.688
After all, this is already part
of their territory.

09:35.901 --> 09:40.619
The two of you are about to battle Autumn
and learn about yourselves.

09:40.994 --> 09:46.506
Once you both come to know each other better...
you'll get several times stronger.

09:47.256 --> 09:51.557
Those are all the hints you get.
Grab the reward by your own hands.

09:52.100 --> 09:54.396
I'm sure the two of you can do it!

09:54.939 --> 09:59.030
Now... let the UMA Autumn arc... begin!

10:02.161 --> 10:03.748
Show me the ultimate ending...

10:04.792 --> 10:07.463
...that I won't see coming!

10:11.639 --> 10:16.398
I knew that'd happen.
It's fine, don't worry.

10:16.691 --> 10:19.572
Look! Your manuscript is safe and sound!

10:19.572 --> 10:23.370
So anyway, anyway! Before you go off
to fight Autumn, let's chat about this here!

10:23.454 --> 10:26.627
There's so much stuff I want to praise
and so much stuff to criticize!

10:26.669 --> 10:29.800
Composition and characters are pretty good,
but line work and figure drawing is terrible.

10:29.800 --> 10:30.844
The art style is too old school...

10:30.927 --> 10:32.054
Still a fan?

10:32.138 --> 10:33.390
Barely.

10:37.691 --> 10:41.824
You'll battle Autumn, learn about yourselves,
and get even stronger!

10:44.997 --> 10:47.544
And I want to help you do just that.

10:48.295 --> 10:49.464
Spill it.

10:50.007 --> 10:52.470
Do you know the future?

10:56.186 --> 11:00.361
And if you do, why did you hide it?
What's your goal?

11:03.910 --> 11:05.622
- Right. Here's your manuscript back.
- Whoa! When did you-

11:05.705 --> 11:07.709
It was a fun read!

11:07.709 --> 11:09.922
Oh, but maybe I should hold onto it?

11:10.381 --> 11:12.176
<i>Teleportation?</i>

11:12.176 --> 11:15.559
<i>A Self-Targeter?
A Voluntary-Type Negator Ability?</i>

11:15.976 --> 11:18.397
<i>Could possibly be an artifact, too.</i>

11:18.940 --> 11:20.610
What a pain.

11:20.986 --> 11:25.119
"Battle with Autumn"?
Do you mean Autumn is here?

11:25.537 --> 11:28.166
Yup. Should be any moment now.

11:29.294 --> 11:30.129
Someone's there!

11:30.755 --> 11:32.341
Hey, wait!
Hold on, Fuko!

11:32.634 --> 11:34.513
Neither of you currently stand a chance!

11:35.347 --> 11:38.437
If you can't fully utilize your powers,
you can't defeat Autumn!

11:38.771 --> 11:39.982
This isn't about winning or losing!

11:40.609 --> 11:43.990
Once a UMA transforms a human,
there's no changing back!

11:44.282 --> 11:45.744
Teacher!

11:46.119 --> 11:48.373
I knew you were still safe, Teacher!

11:51.087 --> 11:54.052
Your arm's hurt.
I'll bandage it for you!

11:57.559 --> 11:58.435
Huh?

11:59.228 --> 12:01.901
T-Thank...

12:03.445 --> 12:04.698
No way.

12:34.424 --> 12:35.467
I understand.

12:45.320 --> 12:46.574
Teacher?

12:46.866 --> 12:47.951
What's wrong?

12:50.289 --> 12:51.416
Teacher!

12:52.627 --> 12:55.340
Teacher!

13:05.612 --> 13:07.866
I need to save more people,
even if just one!

13:08.116 --> 13:14.003
Oh, my. What a pure and selfless line!
So befitting of our protagonist!

13:16.509 --> 13:20.975
I admit, this is the sort of spirit you need
right now to make progress.

13:23.146 --> 13:27.531
But, unless you stop for training on occasion...

13:27.531 --> 13:29.450
...you'll hit walls you won't be able to overcome.

13:31.037 --> 13:32.206
Is that...

13:32.206 --> 13:37.926
Yup. That's Autumn.
A UMA that feeds on human biography.

13:42.476 --> 13:44.313
The guy that just screamed...

13:44.565 --> 13:45.650
There they are!

13:46.067 --> 13:47.319
Please hel-

14:18.633 --> 14:19.676
Oh, no.

14:20.218 --> 14:22.641
It turns people into books and reads them?

14:23.183 --> 14:24.853
Boring.

14:29.821 --> 14:34.246
Give me. Give me.
Give me a story that's truly interesting.

14:41.679 --> 14:46.020
Tell me. Tell me.
Tell me a story no one knows.

14:48.316 --> 14:49.945
Show me. Show me.

14:52.659 --> 14:55.999
Show me a story that's yours alone!

14:56.165 --> 14:58.003
Here it comes!
Grab hold, Fuko!

14:58.003 --> 14:58.713
On it!

15:01.175 --> 15:03.514
Okay, same strategy as with Burn!

15:04.390 --> 15:09.316
I charge up on unluck and enter its body...
deal damage and nab the sucker!

15:18.711 --> 15:21.466
It locked down its body?
Every hole is closed off!

15:21.466 --> 15:22.342
In that case...

15:24.514 --> 15:25.975
I just gotta pry it open!

15:27.687 --> 15:29.900
That won't work.
You lack ideas.

15:31.194 --> 15:33.364
Crimson Bullet!

15:37.582 --> 15:39.418
Not even a scratch!

15:39.418 --> 15:40.337
Andy!

15:43.134 --> 15:44.846
Your leg is turning into books!

15:44.846 --> 15:46.683
No problem, I'll just cut it off!

15:50.398 --> 15:52.737
I just told you that's not going to work.

15:58.289 --> 16:00.753
You both are too caught up in the Rules.

16:01.462 --> 16:06.264
You assume things work in a certain way so much,
you ended up establishing more Rules on your own.

16:08.101 --> 16:11.023
I know it's in a Negator's nature to do so, but...

16:20.585 --> 16:22.087
...if you ask me...

16:22.505 --> 16:27.097
Why would a Negator bind themselves up by Rules?

16:27.807 --> 16:33.318
No matter when, all you need to grow
is proper effort and a flash of inspiration!

16:33.736 --> 16:35.615
Volcano Bullet!

16:36.157 --> 16:37.911
VOLCANO BULLET

16:46.219 --> 16:48.389
What was that?
Did Sensei do that?

16:48.891 --> 16:49.935
Hop on!

17:15.861 --> 17:18.909
That didn't even faze it!
Retreat, retreat!

17:31.852 --> 17:36.152
Phew, that was a close one.
Boy, it sure feels like an adventure!

17:36.653 --> 17:38.574
Hey. That arm of yours comin' back?

17:40.410 --> 17:45.755
Nope. Not at all.
I can only materialize one drawing at a time, after all.

17:46.506 --> 17:48.051
Why would you do this?

17:48.384 --> 17:50.765
Because neither of you would've listened otherwise.

17:52.685 --> 17:56.233
Besides, I'm fine.
I don't need my left hand to draw manga!

17:56.484 --> 18:00.450
Anyway, now that you two are indebted to me,
let's kick off your training arc!

18:04.083 --> 18:06.713
Oopsie! Forgot I don't have my left hand!

18:15.230 --> 18:19.614
Welcome to my humble abode.
It's pretty beat-up, but it's nice and quiet.

18:19.989 --> 18:22.119
Let's head inside and chat.

18:28.172 --> 18:29.718
And this is my work room!

18:32.264 --> 18:38.401
Oh, right! A report!
A report to your boss... about me and Autumn.

18:39.194 --> 18:41.157
<i>They made an Emblem.</i>

18:41.992 --> 18:49.047
So... can I train these two for the sake
of capturing Autumn, and for my sake, Juiz?

18:49.423 --> 18:50.091
Absolutely not.

18:50.425 --> 18:51.051
Wha?

18:51.385 --> 18:56.061
Anno Un, I take it?
I still don't trust you.

18:56.605 --> 19:01.865
What we want is information about the future.
Not some chaos-inducing coach.

19:02.449 --> 19:05.831
My strategy guide only lists the bad ending.

19:06.457 --> 19:11.258
Besides, these two were virtually powerless against Autumn.

19:11.802 --> 19:16.728
I'm sure you have an inkling already?
That unless you take a gamble, there is no future.

19:17.270 --> 19:21.153
These members can make it happen.
Which is why I'm proceeding with caution.

19:21.487 --> 19:25.161
That's backwards. If you have a good hand,
you should go all-in.

19:25.161 --> 19:28.042
What's there to fear when you have a Royal Straight Flush?

19:29.002 --> 19:33.469
I'd hate for you to waste a cast this good on a trite ending.

19:34.137 --> 19:36.977
And I'm sure you feel the same way, Juiz?

19:40.316 --> 19:41.485
Excuse me.

19:41.485 --> 19:42.279
Hm?

19:42.613 --> 19:47.497
- Ms. Juiz, I trust Sensei!
- Why are you screaming into my Emblem?

19:47.497 --> 19:50.253
<i>- You've got one of your own!
- Oh, right! I almost forgot!</i>

19:50.253 --> 19:54.261
<i>- Gah! Now I can't hear out of my left ear!
- I'm sorry!</i>

19:56.641 --> 20:00.983
Well... Sensei risked their life to save us!

20:01.358 --> 20:04.197
I think it's safe to trust such an action!

20:04.489 --> 20:05.910
And I'm askin' ya, too!

20:06.452 --> 20:08.665
This person claims to know about my past.

20:09.166 --> 20:11.880
<i>And there goes my right ear!</i>

20:13.675 --> 20:18.392
The power gap between me and Victor
has always bugged me.

20:18.852 --> 20:23.444
I think the key to closing that gap
is in my past that even I'm unaware of.

20:25.198 --> 20:30.584
I don't know what their training entails.
But if it gets me closer to that key, I wanna try it.

20:33.047 --> 20:34.801
It's so hot.

20:34.884 --> 20:37.598
All right.
Then promise me.

20:38.517 --> 20:39.727
That you'll come back safe...

20:40.813 --> 20:42.692
...and capture Autumn.

20:44.486 --> 20:46.281
Okay, that means...

20:47.492 --> 20:48.954
The deal is sealed!

20:49.914 --> 20:51.584
Is that Autumn's claw?

20:52.252 --> 20:54.549
<i>Autumn turns people into books.</i>

20:55.007 --> 20:59.266
Which means... with this,
you and Fuko here can contact your past.

20:59.642 --> 21:04.986
It's just like you figured!
The key to powering up is in your past, Andy!

21:07.908 --> 21:08.785
Any objections?

21:09.035 --> 21:11.248
Nope. Hurry up and hit me.

21:17.385 --> 21:19.724
Aah... Andy is...

21:20.517 --> 21:21.936
...turning into books?

21:26.111 --> 21:27.030
Wha-

21:43.437 --> 21:44.899
Oh...

21:49.449 --> 21:53.959
TO BE CONTINUED

23:24.055 --> 23:24.974
PREVIEW

23:25.057 --> 23:28.898
<i>The life of the man who can't die
takes shape before the unlucky girl.</i>

23:28.982 --> 23:33.115
<i>That is where the man's "death" lies,
and the girl must know what that is.</i>

23:33.198 --> 23:36.956
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 21-Memento Mori.</i>

23:37.040 --> 23:39.002
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
